<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taedong River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taedong is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> that flows about 450 kilometres south-west from the northern mountains through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-sea">Yellow Sea</a> at Nampo. Its basin was the heartland of late Gojoseon, of the Chinese commandery of Lelang and later of Goguryeo, whose capital Pyongyang stood on its banks from 427.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taedong-river.jpg" alt="Taedong River" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taedong_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
